From: retroforge
Subject: [PATCH] paint the secondary output, direct scanout first

The secondary focus (patch 0041) is now painted on the secondary output
(patch 0040), on every main-loop vblank where it has a new commit and
the output can take a frame (no flip pending).

Direct scanout first: on an unrotated panel, a single opaque buffer the
size of the output goes on the secondary plane as is (each FB is
checked once with a TEST_ONLY commit, the plane may refuse a format or
modifier). Otherwise the frame is composited into one of three
panel-sized images, the composite applying the panel's rotation
(vulkan_composite takes a rotation for override targets; with one
unscaled layer that is the composite-blit rotated copy, which now also
serves such a panel-sized override). The backend holds the queued and
visible FBs, which keeps a client's buffer locked while it is on
screen, and nudges the compositor when a flip completes.

The plane is never asked to rotate: on SM8250, 90/270 planes go through
the one offline SDE rotator (kernel patch 0385), which the main output
already uses and which times its jobs against a single CRTC. (A first
version did rotate there and the main panel stalled; the stall turned
out to be the DPU handing an SSPP from one CRTC to the other, fixed in
kernel patch 0397, but two CRTCs sharing the rotator stay avoided.)

No colour management on that panel. The secondary paint never sets
bPainted, so the main output's repaint state and pacing ignore it. The
debug pattern takes the output back while it is on.

(retroforge: dual-screen boards, step 4 of the dual-output plan, 2026-10-12.)
